# Five of six Dockerfiles here are single-stage `COPY . .`, so whatever is not
# excluded below ships in a layer of a PUBLIC GHCR image (issue #64). The scrub
# cleaned the tree; the change that stops REpublication is this file — an image
# has no business carrying docs, compose files, CI config or agent notes.
#
# This list applies to every Dockerfile in the context, so note two keeps:
# init-db/ stays (Dockerfile.postgres copies it, and src/db/migrations.ts reads
# it at runtime), and public/ stays (the ui and mcp services serve it).

# Build output and installed dependencies — reinstalled inside the image.
node_modules
dist
out
coverage

# Never bake local secrets into an image — every Dockerfile here uses COPY . .
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and CI.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.dockerignore

# Docs, agent instructions, editor config: never read at runtime, and the
# largest surface for a personal detail to ride along into a public layer.
docs
*.md
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Deployment topology describes the operator's hosts, not the container's job.
# The Dockerfile named by -f is always available to the build regardless.
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
.env.example
.mcp.json

# Tests, fixtures and quality tooling. Not runtime code — and fixtures are
# where transcript-shaped personal data most plausibly appears.
**/*.test.ts
src/__tests__
quality
vitest.config.ts
knip.jsonc

# Operator-side helper scripts. Two of them ARE container entrypoints — the
# centroids and warmups images run `pnpm compute:centroids` / `pnpm
# mark:warmups`, and excluding these left both crash-looping on
# ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND. src/quality/dockerfile-entrypoints.test.ts keeps the
# two lists in step.
scripts
!scripts/compute-centroids.ts
!scripts/mark-warmups.ts
*.sh

# Logs
*.log
